1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,131
This tutorial follows one tenancy contract
from the first

2
00:00:03,131 --> 00:00:05,915
draft to its cheques clearing at the bank.

3
00:00:05,915 --> 00:00:08,350
As a Company Admin, open Leasing, then

4
00:00:08,350 --> 00:00:10,786
Tenancy Contracts, and select Draft
Tenancy Contract.

5
00:00:10,786 --> 00:00:14,961
Only vacant units are offered: choose
A-202, then the tenant, Rajesh Kumar.

6
00:00:14,961 --> 00:00:18,440
On Terms, the contract starts on the first
of November,

7
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:21,571
and the end date fills in a year later.

8
00:00:21,571 --> 00:00:24,702
Enter 42,000 as the rent for the full
term,

9
00:00:24,702 --> 00:00:27,486
and set the number of cheques to four.

10
00:00:27,486 --> 00:00:30,269
On Charges, the rent line is already
there,

11
00:00:30,269 --> 00:00:32,704
and its Ledger has filled itself in.

12
00:00:32,704 --> 00:00:36,879
Add a Security Deposit of 4,000 and an
Admin Fee of 1,000.

13
00:00:36,879 --> 00:00:39,663
Each Ledger fills in the moment the charge

14
00:00:39,663 --> 00:00:42,446
is chosen, and the contract value is
47,000.

15
00:00:42,446 --> 00:00:44,882
Save the draft, and generate the cheques.

16
00:00:44,882 --> 00:00:48,709
Separate cheque for one-time charges is
ticked, so the four rent

17
00:00:48,709 --> 00:00:52,536
cheques of 10,500 come with a cheque of
their own for

18
00:00:52,536 --> 00:00:56,363
the deposit, and one for the admin fee,
both dated today.

19
00:00:56,363 --> 00:01:00,190
To put two on one cheque, tick them and
choose Merge.

20
00:01:00,190 --> 00:01:03,669
Generate Cheque Numbers fills every row,
counting up from 600101.

21
00:01:03,669 --> 00:01:06,453
The review runs every check a post would.

22
00:01:06,453 --> 00:01:10,628
It is ready, so select Post Contract, and
the contract is Active.

23
00:01:10,628 --> 00:01:13,759
On its Cheques tab, all six cheques are
registered:

24
00:01:13,759 --> 00:01:16,542
the rent cheques wait for their dates, and

25
00:01:16,542 --> 00:01:19,326
the deposit and fee cheques are due today.

26
00:01:19,326 --> 00:01:22,109
Open Cheque and Cash Collection, then To
deposit,

27
00:01:22,109 --> 00:01:24,892
which lists every cheque whose date has
arrived.

28
00:01:24,892 --> 00:01:27,676
Today's deposit and fee cheques are at the

29
00:01:27,676 --> 00:01:30,111
end: tick both, and choose Deposit Batch.

30
00:01:30,111 --> 00:01:32,547
When the bank confirms, find the deposit

31
00:01:32,547 --> 00:01:34,982
cheque in the register, and choose Clear.

32
00:01:34,982 --> 00:01:38,113
The dialog shows the bank account it
clears into.

33
00:01:38,113 --> 00:01:41,245
Confirm, and it is Cleared, with its
receipt number.

34
00:01:41,245 --> 00:01:43,680
The fee cheque clears the same way.
